  <div class="chapter reveal"><div class="num">Answered</div><div class="orn"><span class="d"></span></div><h2 id="faq">Frequently asked</h2></div>
  <h3 class="reveal">Do I have to leave Skool to do this?</h3>
  <p class="reveal">No. Nothing gets moved out of anywhere. The lessons stay exactly where they are — the site is built underneath them so the same work is reachable from outside as well as inside.</p>
  <h3 class="reveal">How much content do I actually need to start?</h3>
  <p class="reveal">Enough for one article. That's it. The inventory usually turns up far more, but the first block only has to produce a single piece worth rewriting properly.</p>
  <h3 class="reveal">What does the finished site cost to run?</h3>
  <p class="reveal">Roughly a dollar a month, plus the domain. There is no platform subscription underneath it, which is the entire point of owning it.</p>
  <h3 class="reveal">Will Google actually find articles built this way?</h3>
  <p class="reveal">Yes — provided the article genuinely answers something a person is searching for. Indexing is not the hard part. Being worth reading is.</p>
  <h3 class="reveal">Is this the same site you're reading now?</h3>
  <p class="reveal">Yes. Every article in this library started life as a lesson inside a classroom, including this one. Click around — that's the whole demonstration.</p>

